  "reason": "Evidence: config_041 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is the current best at 0.725 acc / 0.685 F1, and we know multi-profile + transformer aggregation + scvi_n200 is the dominant combination. However, we have no direct comparison of fusion method (weighted vs. concat) under the transformer aggregation setting. Question: Does concat fusion match or exceed weighted fusion when paired with transformer aggregation and the best encoders? This isolates a single variable (fusion) from the current best configuration. Why this is the best next experiment: It is the cleanest single-factor extension of our top result, directly testing whether the 0.725 ceiling can be pushed higher on the fusion axis. If concat performs comparably, it confirms weighted is not a binding constraint; if it underperforms, we confirm the current best is near-optimal on that axis and can redirect budget toward the image-encoder question (resnet50 vs. ViT-L)."
}

